From 5313dbe33b590f9dde385b3d90124bbbfeb59c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] Round 8: Hoist the temperature branch and specialize
 exponent lanes

The catchment lane kernel takes the frozen or thawed branch once per
day for the whole group. Valid candidates are partitioned by recharge
exponent: exactly 1 or 2 get a branch-free thawed step that computes
recharge and selects zero on days without liquid water, the value the
scalar path produces by skipping it; other exponents keep the per-lane
check that skips the power call. Lean groups of a known class run eight
lanes, others four, and engine groups grow to eight catchment
candidates. The scalar path composes the same step functions, so
results are bit-identical; new tests cover uniform exponent classes.

An earlier round 8 attempt, sizing worker dispatch by CPUs and batch
work, measured 0.99x on parallel and was reverted (see
evidence/performance-0.3.0/rejected/).

Workload: lean domain (48 catchment scores of 2,400 days), 11 samples
against round 7.
Before median: 0.805 ms. After median: 0.511 ms. Speedup: 1.58x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
